@page "/Error/404"
@layout EmptyLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics

@*
    Static SSR port of Pages/Error/404.cshtml + NotFoundModel (docs/plans/blazor-port-plan.md
    §5 Phase 3). [AllowAnonymous] is required here because Routes.razor's AuthorizeRouteView
    carries a FallbackPolicy that requires authentication globally (docs/architecture/patterns.md
    "Blazor Components"). No @@rendermode - this never needs interactivity.

    Also the target of Routes.razor's new Router.NotFoundPage (this round's only change there):
    the .NET 10 Router renders this component, still through the same route/layout pipeline,
    whenever no route matches or a component calls NavigationManager.NotFound().

    Fidelity fix vs. the cshtml: NotFoundModel.OnGet read HttpContext.Request.Path directly, which
    under UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute is the re-executed error route itself ("/Error/404"), not
    the URL the visitor actually typed - so the "Requested URL" line always showed "/Error/404".
    This reads IStatusCodeReExecuteFeature.OriginalPath (+ OriginalQueryString) instead when the
    re-execute middleware set it, falling back to HttpContext.Request.Path only when that feature
    isn't present (e.g. this component rendered directly for an unmatched Blazor route via
    Router.NotFoundPage, where there was no status-code re-execute).

    App.razor already supplies <!DOCTYPE html>/<head>/<body> (body classes: bg-bg-primary
    text-text-primary font-sans antialiased) for the whole app, so the centering wrapper below is
    a plain <div> rather than the cshtml's own <body> element.

    "Go Back" is a <button data-error-action="back"> wired by wwwroot/js/blazor/error-pages.js
    (a classic script with a document-level delegated click listener) instead of an inline
    onclick="history.back()" - see Forbidden.razor for why.
*@

<PageTitle>Page Not Found - Discord Bot Admin</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <script src="/js/blazor/error-pages.js"></script>
</HeadContent>

<div class="min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center px-4 py-8">
    <div class="w-full max-w-md">
        <!-- Error Icon -->
        <div class="text-center mb-8">
            <div class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-16 h-16 bg-warning rounded-xl mb-4">
                <svg class="w-10 h-10 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z" />
                </svg>
            </div>
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">Page Not Found</h1>
            <p class="text-text-secondary mt-2">The page you're looking for doesn't exist or has been moved.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Message Card -->
        <div class="bg-bg-secondary border border-border-primary rounded-lg p-6 shadow-lg">
            <div class="mb-6 p-4 bg-warning-bg border border-warning-border rounded-lg">
                <p class="text-sm text-warning">
                    <strong>404 Not Found:</strong> This URL doesn't match any resource.
                </p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-sm text-text-primary mb-4">
                The page you requested could not be found. It may have been removed, renamed, or is temporarily unavailable.
            </p>

            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_requestedPath))
            {
                <p class="text-xs text-text-tertiary mb-6 font-mono break-all">
                    Requested URL: @_requestedPath
                </p>
            }

            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-6">
                Please check the URL or navigate back to the dashboard to find what you're looking for.
            </p>

            <div class="flex gap-3">
                <a href="/" class="flex-1 text-center py-2.5 px-4 text-sm font-semibold text-white bg-accent-orange border border-accent-orange rounded-md transition-colors hover:bg-accent-orange-hover hover:border-accent-orange-hover focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-blue focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-bg-secondary">
                    Go to Dashboard
                </a>
                <button type="button" data-error-action="back" class="flex-1 text-center py-2.5 px-4 text-sm font-semibold text-text-primary bg-transparent border border-border-primary rounded-md transition-colors hover:bg-bg-hover focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-blue focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-bg-secondary">
                    Go Back
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private string? _requestedPath;

    // Prerender-only, per "Auth in components" in patterns.md - this page is always static SSR
    // (no @@rendermode), so it is never null while the component actually renders, but the
    // pattern is to null-guard it regardless.
    [CascadingParameter]
    private HttpContext? HttpContext { get; set; }

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        if (HttpContext is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        var reExecuteFeature = HttpContext.Features.Get<IStatusCodeReExecuteFeature>();
        _requestedPath = reExecuteFeature is not null
            ? reExecuteFeature.OriginalPath + reExecuteFeature.OriginalQueryString
            : HttpContext.Request.Path.Value;
    }
}
